                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "237874233",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561197997787139",
                            "num_reviews": 32,
                            "playtime_forever": 953,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 533,
                            "playtime_at_review": 394,
                            "deck_playtime_at_review": 19,
                            "last_played": 1793450868
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This game rules.\n\nAlien Rage is a cover-based shooter with extremely aggressive enemy AI. You're fighting a race of humanoid aliens with a surprisingly varied roster of enemies. You've got invisible enemies that creep up on you with shotguns, huge explosive guys armed with grenade launchers, heavily armoured brutes with miniguns, jetpack troops, and enemies equipped with Quake-style lightning guns that slow you down.\n\nAlthough it's very much a cover shooter, the game is designed to force you to keep moving between cover or eliminate enemies before they overwhelm you. It's quite different from something like Call of Duty, where you can hang back and take your time. This is where much of the game's difficulty comes from.\n\nThe other major source of difficulty is the boss fights. Holy heck, the boss fights in this game are tough. They're those classic FPS boss encounters where you have to shoot glowing weak points while dodging various choreographed attacks. It's a format better suited to something like Doom, and it feels a little out of place in a cover shooter. Despite the challenge, however, the bosses are fun and memorable.\n\nI'd recommend this game to anyone looking for a challenge, particularly people who are really into FPS games. Be warned, though, the game has quite a few glitches. I encountered several during my playthrough, mostly involving boss AI freezing. I also had to edit some configuration files to get the game running smoothly, although there are guides online explaining how to do this.",
